{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3ed9be74-46d8-4f74-ad3d-dfedc695d579","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd9706d3c4206f52","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9004-1z69bxx8/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9004-E001.md","content":"# Disconnected environment installation guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a published disconnected-install guide for KServe raw deployment mode in the product documentation. The KServe capability already exists and works in disconnected clusters; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams currently rediscover the required steps (which images to mirror, which operators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install) through private gists. Source material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and technical review work only — no code, operator, or default-configuration changes.\n\n## Scope\n\nAuthor and publish a disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode covering:\n\n- **Prerequisites**: disconnected cluster requirements, required operators, and the operators that must be skipped in raw deployment mode (the serverless path's mesh/serverless operator dependencies do not apply).\n- **Operator configuration**: how to configure the KServe stack for raw deployment mode on a disconnected cluster.\n- **Image-mirroring reference**: the complete list of required images and the procedure for deriving the digest list per release.\n- **Validation steps**: how to verify a successful air-gapped install (confirming InferenceService readiness in raw deployment mode without mesh dependencies).\n- **Troubleshooting section**: the three most common field-reported failure modes — image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n\nThe content is adapted from existing field enablement material and validated for technical accuracy against the KServe architecture context (raw deployment mode uses plain Deployments/Services with no mesh dependency and is the recommended path for disconnected environments) and reviewed by the RHOAI Serving team. Serverless-mode disconnected support is out of scope and must not appear in the guide.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps.\n- The guide includes a complete image-mirroring reference listing the required images and describing how to derive the digest list per release.\n- The guide includes a troubleshooting section covering image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n- All technical statements in the guide are validated against the KServe architecture context and technically reviewed by the serving team, with review sign-off recorded; the guide contains no serverless-mode instructions and no unsubstantiated claims about disconnected behavior.\n- The guide replaces the need for private gists: a field team can complete a disconnected raw-deployment install using only the published guide.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): disconnected install guide with prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-2 (P1): complete image-mirroring reference with per-release digest derivation — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-3 (P2): troubleshooting section for the three field-reported failure modes — covered by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":19073,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9797304e6164d30d","agent_id":"ac9822f25cae0bb35","session_id":"985b75f6-9e58-4971-b00b-7a17a9fc53e9","uuid":"651e47a4-28fe-4a17-b405-6cff334f7b86","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:15:10.521Z","subagent_type":"general-pu