 deployment mode on a disconnected cluster.\n41\t- **Image-mirroring reference**: the complete list of required images and the procedure for deriving the digest list per release.\n42\t- **Validation steps**: how to verify a successful air-gapped install (confirming InferenceService readiness in raw deployment mode without mesh dependencies).\n43\t- **Troubleshooting section**: the three most common field-reported failure modes — image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n44\t\n45\tThe content is adapted from existing field enablement material and validated for technical accuracy against the KServe architecture context (raw deployment mode uses plain Deployments/Services with no mesh dependency and is the recommended path for disconnected environments) and reviewed by the RHOAI Serving team. Serverless-mode disconnected support is out of scope and must not appear in the guide.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps.\n50\t- The guide includes a complete image-mirroring reference listing the required images and describing how to derive the digest list per release.\n51\t- The guide includes a troubleshooting section covering image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n52\t- All technical statements in the guide are validated against the KServe architecture context and technically reviewed by the serving team, with review sign-off recorded; the guide contains no serverless-mode instructions and no unsubstantiated claims about disconnected behavior.\n53\t- The guide replaces the need for private gists: a field team can complete a disconnected raw-deployment install using only the published guide.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-1 (P1): disconnected install guide with prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps — covered by this epic.\n58\t- HLR-2 (P1): complete image-mirroring reference with per-release digest derivation — covered by this epic.\n59\t- HLR-3 (P2): troubleshooting section for the three field-reported failure modes — covered by this epic.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-943c1ffecfaaa288","agent_id":"a24eac397035d315e","session_id":"985b75f6-9e58-4971-b00b-7a17a9fc53e9","uuid":"276c35ed-8ab9-48d9-9d4b-7d20ec6afda4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:17:08.822Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc0a085f1b45815b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
