corded sign-off. No replacement/rollback or konflux build-pipeline ACs are required (no code change, no konflux chain). No AC states an external schedule constraint. No draft-ID references to sibling epics in the epic body. The final AC (\"a field team can complete a disconnected raw-deployment install using only the published guide\") is a meaningful outcome-based acceptance test tied to the strategy's problem statement.\n35\t\n36\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n37\tEvery strategy scope element is covered: prerequisites, operator configuration (including which operators to skip), image-mirroring reference with per-release digest derivation, validation steps, and the three named failure modes for troubleshooting. Out-of-scope constraints (no code/operator/config changes; no serverless-mode content) are carried into the epic's scope and ACs (\"no serverless-mode instructions\"). Strategy-level context is not dropped: the open-questions status, the field-gist problem, and the source material are all reflected. The strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section declaring documentation support, but a docs-authoring epic exists anyway, so Rule 11 is satisfied trivially. No conditional branches needed.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a44c2c007271853b","agent_id":"a283d4d7b8f47ca7a","session_id":"985b75f6-9e58-4971-b00b-7a17a9fc53e9","uuid":"39ac1869-7579-4656-bd68-fa7b3f603ad4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:19:18.306Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa59922e22392462","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
