{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b44ad81704430952","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9004-E001\n3\ttitle: Disconnected environment installation guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9004\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Docs\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Disconnected environment installation guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a published disconnected-install guide for KServe raw deployment mode in the product documentation. The KServe capability already exists and works in disconnected clusters; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams currently rediscover the required steps (which images to mirror, which operators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install) through private gists. Source material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and technical review work only — no code, operator, or default-configuration changes.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\tAuthor and publish a disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode covering:\n38\t\n39\t- **Prerequisites**: disconnected cluster requirements, required operators, and the operators that must be skipped in raw deployment mode (the serverless path's mesh/serverless operator dependencies do not apply).\n40\t- **Operator configuration**: how to configure the KServe stack for raw deployment mode on a disconnected cluster.\n41\t- **Image-mirroring reference**: the complete list of required images and the procedure for deriving the digest list per release.\n42\t- **Validation steps**: how to verify a successful air-gapped install (confirming InferenceService readiness in raw deployment mode without mesh dependencies).\n43\t- **Troubleshooting section**: the three most common field-reported failure modes — image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n44\t\n45\tThe content is adapted from existing field enablement material and validated for technical accuracy against the KServe architecture context (raw deployment mode uses plain Deployments/Services with no mesh dependency and is the recommended path for disconnected environments) and reviewed by the RHOAI Serving team. Serverless-mode disconnected support is out of scope and must not appear in the guide.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps.\n50\t- The guide includes a complete image-mirroring reference listing the required images and describing how to derive the digest list per release.\n51\t- The guide includes a troubleshooting section covering image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n52\t- All technical statements in the guide are validated against the KServe architecture context and technically reviewed by the serving team, with review sign-off recorded; the guide contains no serverless-mode instructions and no unsubstantiated claims about disconnected behavior.\n53\t- The guide replaces the need for private gists: a field team can complete a disconnected raw-deployment install using only the published guide.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-1 (P1): disconnected install guide with prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps — covered by this epic.\n58\t- HLR-2 (P1): complete image-mirroring reference with per-release digest derivation — covered by this epic.\n59\t- HLR-3 (P2): troubleshooting section for the three field-reported failure modes — covered by this epic.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a44c2c007271853b","agent_id":"a283d4d7b8f47ca7a","session_id":"985b75f6-9e58-4971-b00b-7a17a9fc53e9","uuid":"86e5c7b2-1433-4bc2-a307-bcbacfef5e76","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:19:30.906Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b44ad81704430952","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
